{
  "schema": "perch-native-parity-fixture/1",
  "screen": "files",
  "note": "The Files screen (stock-ui/files) in its two layouts: `explorer`, the tree in the drawer's Files tab (a 300x560 card, the drawer's body), and `editor`, one file's editor in a file tab's pane (760x560). A state's `view.files` is, for workspace `view.workspace`, the workspace's files as the store keeps them (`useWorkspaceFiles`: trees, documents, previews, search, wrap; the web's `useWorkspaceFilesStore` and the native window's store give the same fields); the store's actions do nothing, so nothing is asked of a core. The editor's text is the editor engine's own drawing (CodeMirror on the web): its box is gated, not what it draws. Media states (`image`, `pdf-card`) read the file's bytes from `fixtures/media/` (the web's `workspace-file` URL, served by the reference build; natively the capture's fetch).",
